{"step_index":174,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:56:38Z","content":"When attempting to push, Git prompted for credentials in the terminal (`Username for 'https://github.com':`). \n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **GitHub Authentication Requirements**:\n> GitHub **does not accept account passwords** for Git operations over HTTPS. You must use either a **Personal Access Token (PAT)** or an **SSH Key**.\n\nHere are the two ways to authenticate and complete the push:\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Using a Personal Access Token (HTTPS)\n1. Generate a token on GitHub:\n   * Go to **GitHub → Settings → Developer Settings → Personal access tokens → Tokens (classic)**.\n   * Generate a new token with the **`repo`** scope checked.\n2. Store the credentials in [`~/.git-credentials`](file:///home/koby/.git-credentials):\n   ```bash\n   echo \"https://<USERNAME>:<PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN>@github.com\" >> ~/.git-credentials\n   ```\n3. Once stored, tell me and I will execute `git push origin Baba-Koby` immediately.\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Using an SSH Key (Recommended)\n1. Add your public key to GitHub:\n   * Copy your public key from [`~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub`](file:///home/koby/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub):\n     ```text\n     ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIPOHNo3e4PHToMzflLIq4g/R0dS0Qun98COEu2lPIRU1 koby@debian-trixie\n     ```\n   * Paste it into **GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New SSH key**.\n2. Switch the remote URL to SSH:\n   ```bash\n   git -C /home/koby/LINUX remote set-url origin git@github.com:samyamit-dotcom/LINUX.git\n   ```\n3. Then `git push origin Baba-Koby` will authenticate via your SSH key without prompting for passwords.\n\n---\n\nLet me know which method you prefer or once you have set up the token/key, and I will perform the push!"}
